      "source": [
        "# GARCH Volatility Modeling & VaR Backtesting (with CVaR Forecasting): VCB\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data:** 40 VN-listed equities, daily closing prices, 2023-03-31 to 2026-03-31 (747 trading days)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question:** Can a GARCH(1,1) model with Student-t errors produce well-calibrated one-day-ahead\n",
        "Value-at-Risk forecasts for VCB, and does that calibration hold up across the broader VN equity\n",
        "universe?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Scope note:** VaR forecasts are formally backtested below (Kupiec unconditional-coverage test\n",
        "+ Christoffersen independence test). CVaR (Expected Shortfall) is also forecast at each step, but\n",
        "this notebook does not run a separate ES backtest -- CVaR should be read as a forecast, not as an\n",
        "independently validated number.\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "8a18d317",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-01T14:49:50.125211Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-01T14:49:50.124526Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.771857Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.770420Z"
        },
        "id": "8a18d317"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import scipy.stats as stats\n",
        "from arch import arch_model\n",
        "from statsmodels.stats.diagnostic import het_arch\n",
        "from statsmodels.tsa.stattools import adfuller\n",
        "import warnings\n",
        "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=FutureWarning)\n",
        "\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.precision\", 4)\n",
        "plt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 110\n",
        "\n",
        "TRADING_DAYS_PER_YEAR = 252\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "6461be73",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6461be73"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Data pipeline\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "a8c24725",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.774180Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.773852Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.809745Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.808913Z"
        },
        "id": "a8c24725",
        "outputId": "dcbbffad-5717-4736-c580-270adb183c8e"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "n = 746 trading days (2023-04-03 -> 2026-03-31)\n",
            "Mean: -0.0059%   Std Dev: 1.5007%\n",
            "Skewness: -0.5869   Kurtosis (excess): 13.1873\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "df = pd.read_csv(\"../data/vn_stock_prices_raw.csv\", parse_dates=[\"Date\"])\n",
        "df = df.sort_values(\"Date\").set_index(\"Date\")\n",
        "\n",
        "vcb_price = df[\"VCB\"]\n",
        "log_ret = (np.log(vcb_price / vcb_price.shift(1)).dropna()) * 100  # in percent\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"n = {len(log_ret)} trading days \"\n",
        "      f\"({log_ret.index.min().date()} -> {log_ret.index.max().date()})\")\n",
        "print(f\"Mean: {log_ret.mean():.4f}%   Std Dev: {log_ret.std():.4f}%\")\n",
        "print(f\"Skewness: {log_ret.skew():.4f}   Kurtosis (excess): {log_ret.kurtosis():.4f}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "9852e375",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9852e375"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Descriptive statistics & distributional tests\n",
        "\n",
        "Three formal checks before modeling:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Augmented Dickey-Fuller (ADF) test** -- tests whether the return series is stationary (no\n",
        "  unit root / trend). GARCH modeling assumes a stationary series with a constant unconditional\n",
        "  mean.\n",
        "- **Jarque-Bera test** -- tests whether skewness and kurtosis match a normal distribution.\n",
        "- **ARCH-LM test** -- tests whether squared returns are autocorrelated (large moves cluster\n",
        "  in time).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "885bed14",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.811650Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-01T14:49:51.811416Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.302552Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.301384Z"
        },
        "id": "885bed14",
        "outputId": "331eff52-289a-46a6-fdee-34446f50c0b4"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1760x495 with 3 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 4.5))\n",
        "axes[0].plot(log_ret.index, log_ret.values, linewidth=0.7, color=\"#17324D\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"VCB Daily Log Returns (%)\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Return (%)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].hist(log_ret, bins=50, density=True, color=\"#0E7770\", alpha=0.7, label=\"Empirical\")\n",
        "x = np.linspace(log_ret.min(), log_ret.max(), 200)\n",
        "axes[1].plot(x, stats.norm.pdf(x, log_ret.mean(), log_ret.std()), color=\"#C0392B\",\n",
        "             linewidth=2, label=\"Normal fit\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Return Distribution vs. Normal\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "stats.probplot(log_ret, dist=\"norm\", plot=axes[2])\n",
        "axes[2].set_title(\"Q-Q Plot vs. Normal\")\n",
        "axes[2].get_lines()[0].set_markerfacecolor(\"#0E7770\")\n",
        "axes[2].get_lines()[0].set_markeredgecolor(\"#0E7770\")\n",
        "axes[2].get_lines()[0].set_markersize(4)\n",
        "axes[2].get_lines()[1].set_color(\"#C0392B\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cf2c0154",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cf2c0154"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Reading the Q-Q plot:** If returns were normally distributed, the points would lie close to the red line. Here, the points move away from the line at both ends, showing more extreme negative and positive returns than expected under normality. This suggests that the returns have fat tails, consistent with the Jarque-Bera test.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "6303e540",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.304334Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.304141Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.322029Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.321122Z"
        },
        "id": "6303e540",
        "outputId": "1489a0e7-4214-442a-e49f-cab8565f5bfe"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "ADF statistic: -25.6220   p-value: 0.000000   lags used: 0\n",
            "Critical values: {'1%': np.float64(-3.4391580196774494), '5%': np.float64(-2.8654273226340554), '10%': np.float64(-2.5688400274762397)}\n",
            "-> Reject unit root (series is stationary)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "adf_stat, adf_p, adf_lags, adf_nobs, adf_crit, _ = adfuller(log_ret, autolag=\"AIC\")\n",
        "print(f\"ADF statistic: {adf_stat:.4f}   p-value: {adf_p:.6f}   lags used: {adf_lags}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Critical values: {adf_crit}\")\n",
        "print(\"-> Reject unit root (series is stationary)\" if adf_p < 0.05\n",
        "      else \"-> Cannot reject unit root (series may be non-stationary)\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "71fad03c",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.324144Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.323515Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.331233Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.330363Z"
        },
        "id": "71fad03c",
        "outputId": "2cb963d4-bb1c-423c-f4db-28652b75f11a"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Jarque-Bera: statistic=5369.54, p-value=0.000000\n",
            "-> Reject normality\n",
            "\n",
            "ARCH-LM (5 lags, on raw returns): statistic=39.00, p-value=0.000000\n",
            "-> Significant volatility clustering\n",
            "\n",
            "Note: ARCH-LM is run here on raw returns rather than mean-equation residuals, which is a common simplification when the conditional mean is close to zero (checked in Section 3). A stricter version would test residuals from an explicit mean model.\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "jb_stat, jb_p = stats.jarque_bera(log_ret)\n",
        "print(f\"Jarque-Bera: statistic={jb_stat:.2f}, p-value={jb_p:.6f}\")\n",
        "print(\"-> Reject normality\" if jb_p < 0.05 else \"-> Cannot reject normality\")\n",
        "\n",
        "lm_stat, lm_p, _, _ = het_arch(log_ret, nlags=5)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nARCH-LM (5 lags, on raw returns): statistic={lm_stat:.2f}, p-value={lm_p:.6f}\")\n",
        "print(\"-> Significant volatility clustering\" if lm_p < 0.05 else \"-> No significant ARCH effects\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4a155354",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4a155354"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. GARCH(1,1): Student-t vs. Normal errors\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\sigma_t^2 = \\omega + \\alpha \\, \\epsilon_{t-1}^2 + \\beta \\, \\sigma_{t-1}^2$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Given the heavy tails found above, we fit **both** a Normal-GARCH and a Student-t-GARCH and\n",
        "compare them on log-likelihood, AIC, and BIC -- rather than just asserting Student-t is better,\n",
        "we check.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "943a8f47",
      "metadata": {
        "execution": {
          "iopub.execute_input": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.332990Z",
          "iopub.status.busy": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.332689Z",
          "iopub.status.idle": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.377457Z",
          "shell.execute_reply": "2026-09-01T14:49:52.376576Z"
        },
        "id": "943a8f47",
        "outputId": "bd99f686-0d37-48ad-abda-65a7bca17ab6"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "text/html": [
              "<div>\n",
              "<style scoped>\n",
              "    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n",
              "        vertical-align: middle;\n",
              "    }\n",
              "\n",
              "    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n",
              "        vertical-align: top;\n",
              "    }\n",
              "\n",
