      "source": [
        "**This is the headline result of the notebook, now computed from the corrected daily-refit\n",
        "backtest rather than the earlier buggy version.** The pass/fail counts printed above are read\n",
        "directly from this run -- they are not retyped or assumed from any prior draft. The gap between\n",
        "the Kupiec-only pass rate and the conditional-coverage pass rate (if any) is itself informative:\n",
        "a stock can have roughly the right *number* of breaches while still failing conditional coverage\n",
        "if those breaches cluster in time, which Kupiec alone cannot detect.\n",
        "\n",
        "The broader conclusion from Section 8 stands regardless of the exact numbers: **a single fixed\n",
        "GARCH(1,1)-t specification does not calibrate equally well across every VN stock**, and checking\n",
        "this required the corrected, non-stale walk-forward backtest above -- a production risk system\n",
        "built this way would need per-asset validation, not a single backtest assumed to generalize.\n"
      ]
